    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250-a4">

                <pb facs="0462" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg362"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    773.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fernandez to Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department for Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 17,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have received your excellency’s
                    note of the 13th instant, relating to the imprisonment at Coatzacoalcos of Mr.
                    Howard C. Walker, accused, as it is reported, of having stolen wood.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say to your excellency that I have this day asked
                    for information upon the subject from the governor of Vera Cruz.</p>
                <p>I renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOSÉ FERNANDEZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
